//! stage:typing no-std
// attack (review): the joint reading also selects a witness of a later layer. 'A is P' has a one-step
// witness (X = C, not Q) and a two-step witness through a conditional given (X = B, Q). Alone, the
// one-step witness is the result. Needs assocsubst for the projection through the conditional given.
// expected (premsubst + commit rule): rejected. expected (joint reading, with assocsubst): accepted.
// observed: (eq25, premsubst as first designed) FULL+premsubst rejected (bound=1 released=2 normalized=1); +selfcheck same; +assocsubst accepted; NEW accepted
// currently: base rejected (subgoals=7 matches=453): no coercion from '(P<A>, Q<(A::P).X>) ==> [Void]() let -> Void' to '[Void]() let -> Void'; FULL rejected (subgoals=5 matches=82): no coercion from '(P<A>, Q<(A::P).X>) ==> [Void]() let -> Void' to '[Void]() let -> Void'
trait P { type X }
trait Q {}
struct A {}
struct B {}
struct C {}
struct N<T> {}
given B is Q {}
given A is P { type X = C }
given N<A> is P { type X = B }
given <where N<A> is P> => A is P { type X = B }
fun f<T where T is P, T.X is Q>() {}
public fun main() { f<A>() }
